			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Demo: RTPProxy beyond audio forwarding</title>
				<link>https://www.rtpproxy.org/post/2022-opensips-summit-demo/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 29 Sep 2022 06:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://www.rtpproxy.org/post/2022-opensips-summit-demo/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RTPProxy: beyond audio forwarding. DTMF processing, Video calling and some other advanced functions yet to be released&lt;/strong&gt;, by Maksym Sobolyev, at OpenSIPS Summit 2022 in Athens.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An interactive demo of the RTPProxy functionality beyond audio forwarding. It is the first demo in the recording of the interactive demos day of the summit.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;iframe allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen&#34; loading=&#34;eager&#34; referrerpolicy=&#34;strict-origin-when-cross-origin&#34; src=&#34;https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/e5HCn-7u1hQ?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; title=&#34;RTPProxy: beyond audio forwarding. DTMF processing, Video calling and some other advanced functions yet to be released&#34;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e5HCn-7u1hQ&#34;&gt;Watch on YouTube&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Talk: Sippy Labs Update - RTPProxy, OpenSIPIt and Microsippy</title>
				<link>https://www.rtpproxy.org/post/2020-opensips-summit/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2020 07:06:39 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://www.rtpproxy.org/post/2020-opensips-summit/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sippy Labs Update - RTPProxy, OpenSIPIt and Microsippy&lt;/strong&gt;, by Maksym Sobolyev, at OpenSIPS Summit 2020 (online).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An overview of the latest activities at Sippy in the open-source SIP space, covering:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;RTPProxy 2.2: what&amp;rsquo;s new? Road towards RTPProxy 3.0;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Microsippy (very small-scale SIP): where are we, what&amp;rsquo;s next?;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;OpenSIPIt 2020: &amp;ldquo;Stirring but not Shaking&amp;rdquo;. Open SIP interoperability testing, from idea to implementation.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;div style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;iframe allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen&#34; loading=&#34;eager&#34; referrerpolicy=&#34;strict-origin-when-cross-origin&#34; src=&#34;https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/rOmBc62ypjY?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; title=&#34;Sippy Labs Update - RTPProxy, OpenSIPIt and Microsippy&#34;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rOmBc62ypjY&#34;&gt;Watch on YouTube&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Talk: Designing a Better Real-Time Media Control Protocol</title>
				<link>https://www.rtpproxy.org/post/2019-januscon/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 27 Sep 2019 07:47:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://www.rtpproxy.org/post/2019-januscon/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Designing a Better Real-Time Media Control Protocol for a Smarter World&lt;/strong&gt;, by Maksym Sobolyev, at JanusCon 2019.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The RTPProxy has seen quite a lot of adoption in the telco world in the last 15 years, in a big part thanks to some of the key decisions around designing and extending its control protocol. There are some challenges that require a near-complete overhaul to provide for previously unforeseen scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;iframe allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen&#34; loading=&#34;eager&#34; referrerpolicy=&#34;strict-origin-when-cross-origin&#34; src=&#34;https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/vhk6Um_fEL4?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; title=&#34;Designing a Better Real-Time Media Control Protocol for a Smarter World&#34;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vhk6Um_fEL4&#34;&gt;Watch on YouTube&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
